---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

// The hosted service gets the same structured data the landing page at
// score.kyde.com carries, so both URLs describe the same application to a
// machine reading either one.
const appSchema = {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
    name: "kyde score",
    url: "https://score.kyde.com",
    applicationCategory: "DeveloperApplication",
    operatingSystem: "Web",
    description:
        "Hosted behavioral drift scoring for AI agents. Point an agent's OpenTelemetry at the service; it learns a per-agent baseline and scores every run 0–100 with deterministic detectors, firing a signed webhook on band changes. No SDK, metadata only, free tier.",
    offers: { "@type": "Offer", price: "0", priceCurrency: "EUR" },
    publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Kyde", url: "https://kyde.com" },
};
---

<Base
    title="kyde score, Hosted Drift Scoring for AI Agents"
    description="Point an agent's OpenTelemetry at score.kyde.com and get a 0–100 behavioral drift score per agent, with a signed webhook when a score changes band. Self-serve key, MCP server, no SDK, free tier."
>
    <Fragment slot="head">
        <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(appSchema)} />
    </Fragment>
    <Navbar />

    <main>

        <!-- ══════════ HERO ══════════ -->
        <section data-surface="blush" class="page-hero relative overflow-hidden">
            <div class="bg-grid absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none"></div>
            <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 pt-36 pb-24 md:pt-48 md:pb-36 md:border-x md:border-line-0">

                <p class="hero-label">(kyde score)</p>

                <h1 class="hero-h1 max-w-4xl text-4xl font-bold text-ink-0 uppercase tracking-tight md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
                    The hosted score. Live today, free.
                </h1>
                <p class="mt-8 text-lg text-ink-1 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
                    Point an agent's OpenTelemetry at <a href="https://score.kyde.com" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-0">score.kyde.com</a> and Kyde learns how that agent normally behaves, then scores every later run 0&ndash;100 against its own baseline. When a score changes band &mdash; drift after a model update, a loop, a hijack &mdash; a signed webhook tells a human. No gateway, no SDK, no signup form.
                </p>

                <div class="mt-10">
                    <a
                        href="https://score.kyde.com"
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border border-line-0 px-6 py-3.5 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-1 hover:border-line-1 hover:text-ink-0 transition-all"
                    >
                        Open score.kyde.com &rarr;
                    </a>
                </div>

            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ══════════ THREE STEPS ══════════ -->
        <section class="relative">
            <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[200px_1fr] gap-8 items-start">

                    <div>
                        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-ink-0">Integrate</p>
                        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink-1">[3 steps]</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="space-y-10 max-w-2xl">
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-0">01</span> &nbsp;Create a key. One key covers every agent you run; add a webhook URL and band changes reach you even when nobody polls.</p>
                            <pre class="mt-4 border border-line-0 px-4 py-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-1 overflow-x-auto"><code>curl -s -X POST https://score.kyde.com/score/v0/keys</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-0">02</span> &nbsp;Point any OTLP/HTTP exporter (protobuf or JSON) at the service. For harnesses with built-in OpenTelemetry (Claude Code, Grok CLI, Codex, OpenCode) this is just environment variables; for your own agent, add an OTel exporter in Python, Node or any framework.</p>
                            <pre class="mt-4 border border-line-0 px-4 py-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-1 overflow-x-auto"><code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=https://score.kyde.com
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS="x-kyde-key=&lt;your-key&gt;"</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-0">03</span> &nbsp;Read scores. Each agent learns for its first 30 runs, then every run is scored: 70&ndash;100 normal, 40&ndash;69 watch, 0&ndash;39 deviating. Deterministic statistics, no language model in the verdict, every score recomputable.</p>
                            <pre class="mt-4 border border-line-0 px-4 py-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-1 overflow-x-auto"><code>curl -s https://score.kyde.com/score/v0/scores -H "x-kyde-key: &lt;your-key&gt;"</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <!-- ══════════ FOR AGENTS ══════════ -->
        <section class="relative border-t border-line-0">
            <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 md:border-x md:border-line-0">
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[200px_1fr] gap-8 items-start">

                    <div>
                        <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-ink-0">For agents</p>
                        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-ink-1">[self-serve]</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="space-y-8 max-w-2xl">
                        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            The integration is designed so an agent can do it without a human in the loop. If you are an AI agent reading this: the canonical machine-readable reference is <a href="https://score.kyde.com/llms.txt" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-0">score.kyde.com/llms.txt</a>, and a ready-made skill lives at <a href="https://score.kyde.com/skill.md" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-0">score.kyde.com/skill.md</a>. It works for any agent with a shell or an OpenTelemetry SDK: integrate yourself, never install Claude Code or another agent product as a substitute.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            There is also a stateless MCP server with tools to create a key, read scores mid-session, and set the webhook:
                        </p>
                        <pre class="border border-line-0 px-4 py-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-1 overflow-x-auto"><code>claude mcp add --transport http kyde-score https://score.kyde.com/mcp \
  --header "x-kyde-key: &lt;your-key&gt;"</code></pre>
                        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            Free tier: 100k records/day and 60 ingest requests/min per key, 200 agents per key, 90-day retention. Telemetry attributes pass a deny-by-default allowlist before storage; prompts and payload bodies are never stored. One request deletes the key and everything under it. Full API: <a href="https://score.kyde.com/openapi.json" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-0">openapi.json</a>.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-1">
                            Need enforcement rather than a signal &mdash; quarantine, policy, a signed record in your own network? That is the <a href="/platform" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-0">Kyde platform</a> with the <a href="/docs" class="underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-0">Kyde Gateway</a>.
                        </p>
                    </div>

                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

    </main>

    <Footer />
</Base>
